  "records": [
    {"anchor":"U00995","actual_pdf_page_and_row":"40, row 5","observed_before":"ལོ་ནི་བདུན་ཅུ་རྩ་ལྔར་འཛིན","observed_target":"དེ་ཡི་རྗེས་སུ་སྐལ་ལྡན་པ","observed_after":"སོ་ཤའི་གླིང་ཞེས","detached_boundary_shads":3,"terminal_tsheg":false,"observed_sign_description":"After the final པ, two closely spaced upright strokes are detached from the letter. Across the following blank interval, a third upright stands immediately before སོ. All three occupy the target row; none is a stroke from the row above or below.","existing_reading":"དེ་ཡི་རྗེས་སུ་སྐལ་ལྡན་པ།","punctuation_only_proposal":"Preserve combined boundary པ།། །སོ: two target-adjacent shads and one following-leading shad.","confidence":"High for correspondence and boundary count.","uncertainty":"Electronic ownership of the third shad is editorial; its physical presence is clear.","correspondence_confirmed":true},
    {"anchor":"U01094","actual_pdf_page_and_row":"44, rows 3 / 4; terminal boundary in row 4","observed_before":"གོང་མའི་ལུས་དང་ཡན་ལག་རྫོགས","observed_target":"ལུས་རྫོགས་ཡན་ལག་གསང་ / འབྱེད་པའོ","observed_after":"གཉིས་པའི་ལུས་ནི","detached_boundary_shads":2,"terminal_tsheg":false,"observed_sign_description":"The target begins at the right of row 3 and continues at the left of row 4. One detached upright follows པའོ; another stands after a blank interval immediately before གཉིས. The vowel above the terminal letter and the adjacent-row strokes are excluded.","existing_reading":"ལུས་རྫོགས་ཡན་ལག་གསང་འབྱེད་པའོ།","punctuation_only_proposal":"Preserve combined boundary པའོ། །གཉིས; retain the following-leading shad if units are stored separately.","confidence":"High for correspondence and boundary count.","uncertainty":"Nearby small source writing is not transcribed or reassigned. No material uncertainty in the two boundary shads.","correspondence_confirmed":true},
    {"anchor":"U01270","actual_pdf_page_and_row":"50, row 6","observed_before":"གཞན་ནི་མཉམ་པའི་སྦྱོར་བ་ཉིད","observed_target":"རྣལ་འབྱོར་པ་ཡིས་བརྩམ་པར་བྱའོ","observed_after":"དྲིས་ལན","detached_boundary_shads":2,"terminal_tsheg":false,"observed_sign_description":"One detached vertical follows the terminal བྱའོ. A second vertical stands immediately before the smaller following heading beginning དྲིས་ལན. Both are above and separate from the lower frame line; the terminal letter's curved strokes are not counted.","existing_reading":"རྣལ་འབྱོར་པ་ཡིས་བརྩམ་པར་བྱའོ།","punctuation_only_proposal":"Preserve combined boundary བྱའོ། །དྲིས; count the heading-leading shad as well as the target-adjacent shad.","confidence":"High for local correspondence and boundary count; limited for the complete heading.","uncertainty":"The heading is quoted only through its legible opening; its remaining wording is not certified. Additional writing after the quoted preceding phrase is outside that quotation and is not reassigned.","correspondence_confirmed":true},
    {"anchor":"U01416","actual_pdf_page_and_row":"56, row 4","observed_before":"འབྱུང་བའི་ཡི་གེ་རབ་བཟླས་ཤིང་","observed_target":"ལུས་ཀྱི་གནས་ལྔར་ལེགས་སྤྱོད་ན","observed_after":"འབྱུང་བའི་དུས་ཉིད","detached_boundary_shads":2,"terminal_tsheg":false,"observed_sign_description":"The final ན has its own descending right stroke. Beyond it is one separate upright shad; across a wider space is another upright immediately before འབྱུང. These are two detached signs, independently of the final-letter stroke.","existing_reading":"ལུས་ཀྱི་གནས་ལྔར་ལེགས་སྤྱོད་ན།","punctuation_only_proposal":"Preserve combined boundary ན། །འབྱུང; retain both physical shads.","confidence":"High for correspondence and boundary count.","uncertainty":"No material uncertainty in the local sign inventory; ownership between electronic units is not determined by spacing alone.","correspondence_confirmed":true},
    {"anchor":"U01534","actual_pdf_page_and_row":"60, row 6 / 61, row 1; terminal boundary on page 61, row 1","observed_before":"དངོས་གཞི་རང་གི་རྒྱུད་བརྟེན་ནི","observed_target":"ལུས་ཀྱི་ / གནད་དང་ངག་དང་ཡང་","observed_after":"སེམས་ཀྱི་གནད་ལ་བརྟེན་པ་ཡིས","detached_boundary_shads":2,"terminal_tsheg":true,"observed_sign_description":"The target begins at the right of page 60's last row and resumes on page 61's first row. After final ང, a small detached upper tsheg precedes the target-adjacent shad. A second shad stands across the blank interval immediately before སེམས. Page-opening ornament and strokes from row 2 are excluded.","existing_reading":"ལུས་ཀྱི་གནད་དང་ངག་དང་ཡང་།","punctuation_only_proposal":"Preserve combined boundary ཡང་། །སེམས: one terminal tsheg and two shads.","confidence":"High for correspondence and shad count; moderately high for the small terminal tsheg.","uncertainty":"The tsheg is much smaller than the two uprights but is distinguishable as a separate upper mark. Page-break ornaments and fillers are not inventoried.","correspondence_confirmed":true}
  ],
  "scope_limitations": ["Native pages inspected before context and terminal crops. Local boundaries only; no whole-page certification.", "Page numbers follow the supplied attachment metadata. Rows count main text rows from the top.", "Observed quotations are bounded excerpts. Boundary shads are inventoried separately; / denotes a physical row or page split, not a source sign.", "Electronic allocation must preserve the combined physical inventory. Small annotations, adjacent-row strokes, frame lines and final-letter strokes are excluded.", "No tools, network, filesystem access or writes. This is neither translation nor human palaeographic certification."]
